IMPORTANT: This is an implementation/fix request, not a request to redesign the game from scratch. Preserve the existing visual style, navigation structure, game logic, assets, naming, and gameplay that we have already built unless I explicitly ask you to change something.

I need you to carefully inspect the existing project/GitHub source before making changes. Do not invent replacement content when the existing project already contains the correct content.

There are several connected issues that must be fixed together. Please treat this as ONE coherent progression/navigation system.

==================================================
1. IMPORTANT: USE THE EXISTING GAME MODES
==================================================

We already built four gameplay modes previously.

Use the SAME gameplay modes we already built, with the SAME names/labels and the SAME underlying gameplay implementation.

Do NOT create new substitute modes.
Do NOT rename them.
Do NOT redesign them.

The four existing modes are:

1. Multiple-choice mode
2. Combining words into a sentence
3. Combining letters into a word
4. The Tetris-like mode

The Tetris-like mode is the PREMIUM/PAID mode.

The first three modes are available to free players.
The fourth/Tetris-like mode must remain visible but locked/greyed out for free players.

This is intentional because showing the locked premium mode is part of the game's motivation to upgrade.

IMPORTANT:
These gameplay modes should NOT appear as separate tabs on the Home page.

They should appear INSIDE the player's progression after:
Continue Your Journey → Lesson → appropriate Minion → choose gameplay mode.

The existing main navigation should remain the same:

Home
Play
Item Shop
Achievements
Leaderboard

Do NOT add a new permanent "Modes" tab or "Lessons" tab to the main navigation.

==================================================
2. FIX THE CONTINUE YOUR JOURNEY FLOW
==================================================

The current flow is WRONG.

Right now:

Continue Your Journey
→ Lesson 1
→ Lesson 2
→ Lesson 3
→ Tower/map page

That is NOT what we want.

The correct flow is:

Continue Your Journey
→ Lesson 1
→ dedicated gameplay-mode selection page
→ Minion 1
→ Lesson 2
→ dedicated gameplay-mode selection page
→ Minion 2
→ Lesson 3
→ dedicated gameplay-mode selection page
→ Minion 3
→ Boss 1

Then the same structure continues for Boss 2, Boss 3, Boss 4, and Boss 5.

The player should NEVER simply be pushed automatically from Lesson 1 to Lesson 2 to Lesson 3 without interacting with the game progression.

The lessons and combat/gameplay progression must be connected.

==================================================
3. EXACT PROGRESSION STRUCTURE
==================================================

For the initial launch version, use:

15 lessons
5 bosses
3 minions per boss

Therefore:

Boss 1 chapter:
Lesson 1
→ Minion 1
Lesson 2
→ Minion 2
Lesson 3
→ Minion 3
→ Boss 1

Boss 2 chapter:
Lesson 4
→ Minion 1
Lesson 5
→ Minion 2
Lesson 6
→ Minion 3
→ Boss 2

Boss 3 chapter:
Lesson 7
→ Minion 1
Lesson 8
→ Minion 2
Lesson 9
→ Minion 3
→ Boss 3

Boss 4 chapter:
Lesson 10
→ Minion 1
Lesson 11
→ Minion 2
Lesson 12
→ Minion 3
→ Boss 4

Boss 5 chapter:
Lesson 13
→ Minion 1
Lesson 14
→ Minion 2
Lesson 15
→ Minion 3
→ Boss 5

This gives us exactly:

15 lessons = 3 lessons × 5 bosses
15 minion encounters = 3 minions × 5 bosses
5 bosses

This is the progression structure for the CURRENT launch version.

Do NOT remove bosses to make the free version fit.
Do NOT change Boss 5 into Boss 2.
Do NOT renumber the lore.
Do NOT restructure the existing five-boss story.

The current decision is to keep all five bosses and provide 15 lessons for the initial version.

A future major update can expand this system with additional lessons, bosses, gameplay, and lore. Do NOT build that future expansion now.

==================================================
4. FREE VS PAID PROGRESSION
==================================================

The free version should allow the player to experience the intended beginning of the progression.

The Tetris-like gameplay mode is the premium restriction.

When a free player reaches a minion and sees the four gameplay modes:

Mode 1 = available
Mode 2 = available
Mode 3 = available
Mode 4 / Tetris-like = visible but greyed out and locked

If the player clicks the locked Tetris-like mode, clearly explain that this mode requires the full paid version.

Do NOT hide the Tetris-like mode.

The locked mode is intentionally visible because it is part of the game's upgrade motivation.

The paid/full version unlocks the Tetris-like mode throughout the progression.

Also preserve the existing full-trial behavior that was recently restored.

==================================================
5. MODE SELECTION MUST BE A FULL PAGE, NOT A POPUP
==================================================

This is VERY IMPORTANT.

Currently, after the third lesson, Claude added a popup asking the player to choose a mode.

That is NOT acceptable.

Do NOT use a popup/modal for gameplay-mode selection.

Create a dedicated FULL PAGE for gameplay-mode selection.

Reason:

If the player accidentally clicks outside the popup, the current implementation can leave the player stuck and they have to refresh/replay the lessons.

A dedicated page eliminates that problem.

The page should clearly show the four existing gameplay modes and allow the player to choose one.

The player can safely navigate/select from this page without losing progression.

The page should know which minion the player is about to face.

Example:

Lesson 1 completed
→ "Choose how you want to face Minion 1"
→ four gameplay modes
→ player selects one
→ Minion 1 gameplay begins

After completing Minion 1:
→ continue to Lesson 2

After Lesson 2:
→ mode-selection page for Minion 2

After Minion 2:
→ Lesson 3

After Lesson 3:
→ mode-selection page for Minion 3

After Minion 3:
→ Boss 1

Use the existing mode names exactly as they already exist in the project.

==================================================
6. MINIONS MUST ACTUALLY BE PROGRESSION-LOCKED
==================================================

There is currently a serious state/progression bug.

The first three minions appear GREEN/completed immediately, even though this is a fresh browser/session and the player has never played them.

That is WRONG.

"Minions" here means the regular, weaker enemies that appear before the boss.

They are NOT minibosses.

They are weaker enemies with lower health/health points than the boss.

The initial state must be:

Minion 1 = grey/locked or available according to the current progression state
Minion 2 = grey/locked
Minion 3 = grey/locked
Boss = locked

The player must be the one who changes their state through actual progression.

For a fresh player:

Lesson 1 completed
→ Minion 1 becomes available

Player completes Minion 1
→ Minion 1 becomes GREEN/completed
→ Minion 2 becomes available

Player completes Minion 2
→ Minion 2 becomes GREEN/completed
→ Minion 3 becomes available

Player completes Minion 3
→ Minion 3 becomes GREEN/completed
→ Boss becomes available

Player completes Boss 1
→ Boss 1 becomes GREEN/completed
→ next chapter becomes available

Do NOT initialize the first three minions as completed.

Do NOT hard-code them as green.

Their state must be derived from the player's actual progression/progress data.

A fresh browser/new player should NOT inherit completed minions.

Please inspect the existing progression-state logic and fix the underlying cause instead of simply changing the visual color.

==================================================
7. LESSON PROGRESSION GAUGE
==================================================

We now have a "Your Lessons" progression section on the Home page, similar to "Your Tower."

Keep that concept.

The Home page should contain:

Your Tower / برجك
and
Your Lessons / دروسك

The Lessons progression should visually match the Tower progression system.

There should be 15 lesson progression segments for the current launch version.

The progression should be segmented/discrete, not one continuous bar.

Just like the Tower progression shown in the screenshots.

Each lesson corresponds to one segment.

As the player progresses, completed lesson segments should change color.

IMPORTANT:

The color change should NOT be a random color jump.

I specifically do NOT want something visually nonsensical like yellow → pink or unrelated colors.

Use a coherent two-color progression spectrum/gradient.

For example, a warm progression such as:

yellow → orange → red

or another visually logical progression between two recognizable main colors.

The exact palette can be chosen to fit the existing game's design, but the progression must visually make sense.

Do NOT use unrelated colors.

The same principle should be applied consistently to the Tower progression and Lessons progression.

The screenshots show that the segmented progression concept itself is good. Keep that.

==================================================
8. CLICKING "YOUR LESSONS" MUST OPEN A REAL PAGE
==================================================

Currently clicking Lessons opens a popup/list, but the list is essentially useless because the player cannot properly access the lessons.

Fix this.

When the player clicks/touches "Your Lessons / دروسك", redirect them to a FULL PAGE.

Do NOT use a popup.

Do NOT create a new permanent main-navigation tab.

The existing main navigation remains:

Home
Play
Item Shop
Achievements
Leaderboard

The Lessons page is a destination reached from the Home page's "Your Lessons" progression component.

On the Lessons page, show the complete lesson progression/list.

The player must be able to:

- see all 15 lessons
- see which lessons have been completed
- see which lesson is currently available
- see which lessons are locked
- click/touch lessons that they are allowed to revisit
- revisit completed lessons
- access available lessons
- understand why future lessons are locked

Do NOT merely display the list as decorative text.

The lesson entries must actually be functional.

Use the real lesson names/content from the existing project.

==================================================
9. IMPORTANT: TRANSFER/USE ALL EXISTING LESSON CONTENT
==================================================

THIS IS A DIRECT IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENT.

Inspect the GitHub/project source and locate ALL existing lesson content/data that has already been created.

Transfer/integrate ALL of those existing lessons into the actual game.

Do NOT create placeholder lessons.
Do NOT create fake lesson names.
Do NOT show an empty lesson list.
Do NOT omit existing lesson content.

The lessons that already exist in GitHub must be properly connected to the game's lesson system and displayed/usable inside the game.

The lesson list should be populated from the real existing lesson data.

If the project already contains lesson IDs, names, questions, vocabulary, grammar content, exercises, etc., reuse those structures instead of duplicating or inventing them.

Before finishing, verify that the lesson data actually appears in the playable game.

