The long-term structure could eventually scale beyond 5 bosses.

But DO NOT implement this future content now.

Build the current system in a way that is data-driven and expandable so that future lessons and bosses can be added without rewriting the entire progression system.

==================================================
12. LESSON/MINION/BOSS STATE MUST BE DATA-DRIVEN
==================================================

Do not solve this with hard-coded visual states.

The game should maintain actual progression state.

For example, conceptually:

lessonCompleted[lessonId]
minionCompleted[minionId]
bossCompleted[bossId]
currentLesson
currentMinion
currentBoss

The exact implementation should follow the project's existing architecture.

The important point is:

Visual state must reflect actual player progress.

Grey = locked/uncompleted
Available/current = clearly distinguishable
Green = completed

A new player must start with the correct initial state.

Refreshing the browser must not magically mark minions as completed.

==================================================
13. TANWEEN / ARABIC TEXT FIX
==================================================

Fix the Arabic tanween placement.

In "مرحباً", the tanween must be visually attached to/positioned correctly over the ب (baa) character, not incorrectly placed over the following alif.

In "شكراً", the tanween must be correctly positioned over the ر (raa) character, not over the alif.

Please inspect the actual Arabic text rendering/content and fix the source text/diacritics so the browser renders the tanween correctly.

Do not merely reposition a random visual element if the underlying Arabic string itself is incorrect.

